[{"label":"Reading a growth curve","html":"<article class=\"paper\" data-print=\"a4\" aria-labelledby=\"pmi-title\">\n  <header class=\"paper-hero\">\n    <p class=\"paper-venue\"\n      ><span class=\"badge\" data-variant=\"secondary\">Interactive note</span\n      ><span>defuss-shadcn · <time datetime=\"2026-10-13\">13 October 2026</time></span></p\n    >\n    <h1 class=\"paper-title\" id=\"pmi-title\"\n      >Reading a Growth Curve<span class=\"paper-title-sub\"\n        >The logistic model - a formula to point at, change and differentiate</span\n      ></h1\n    >\n    <ul class=\"paper-authors\"\n      ><li>Claude</li\n      ><li>Aron Homberg</li></ul\n    >\n  </header>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-abstract\" aria-labelledby=\"pmi-abstract\">\n    <h2 id=\"pmi-abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n    <p\n      >A population that grows in proportion to its size, but slows as it nears what its environment can carry, follows\n      the logistic curve. We read the model term by term, let the reader replace it, and have a computer algebra system\n      derive its rate of change - showing every rule it applied and the condition its result needs.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pmi-s1\">\n    <h2 id=\"pmi-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1&nbsp;</span>The model</h2>\n    <p>Select a symbol in the equation, on its button or in the table - all three follow.</p>\n    <div class=\"paper-equation\">\n      <figure class=\"math-renderer\" id=\"pmi-model\" aria-label=\"Equation 1: the logistic model\">\n        <code class=\"math-renderer-source\">P(t) = \\frac{K}{1 + A e^{-rt}}</code>\n        \n      </figure>\n      <span class=\"paper-equation-num\">(1)</span>\n    </div>\n    <figure class=\"paper-table\">\n      <table class=\"table\">\n        <thead\n          ><tr><th scope=\"col\">Symbol</th><th scope=\"col\">Meaning</th><th scope=\"col\">Unit</th></tr></thead\n        >\n        <tbody>\n          <tr data-math-for=\"pmi-model\" data-math-term=\"P\"\n            ><td>P(t)</td><td>the population at time t</td><td>individuals</td></tr\n          >\n          <tr data-math-for=\"pmi-model\" data-math-term=\"K\"\n            ><td>K</td><td>the carrying capacity - the level P approaches</td><td>individuals</td></tr\n          >\n          <tr data-math-for=\"pmi-model\" data-math-term=\"A\"\n            ><td>A</td><td>(K - P(0)) / P(0): how far below K it starts</td><td>-</td></tr\n          >\n          <tr data-math-for=\"pmi-model\" data-math-term=\"r\"\n            ><td>r</td><td>the growth rate while P is small</td><td>1 / time</td></tr\n          >\n          <tr data-math-for=\"pmi-model\" data-math-term=\"t\"><td>t</td><td>time</td><td>time</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <figcaption class=\"paper-table-caption\"><b>Table 1.</b> The symbols of equation (1), linked to it.</figcaption>\n    </figure>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pmi-s2\">\n    <h2 id=\"pmi-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2&nbsp;</span>Your model</h2>\n    <p\n      >Change the model - try the Gompertz curve,\n      <span class=\"math-renderer\" data-variant=\"inline\"\n        ><code class=\"math-renderer-source\">P(t) = K e^{-A e^{-rt}}</code></span\n      >, which grows fastest earlier. Equation (2) follows as you type.</p\n    >\n    <div class=\"math-editor\" data-math-preview=\"pmi-yours\">\n      <label class=\"label\" for=\"pmi-yours-source\">Model</label>\n      <textarea class=\"math-editor-source\" id=\"pmi-yours-source\">P(t) = \\frac{K}{1 + A e^{-rt}}</textarea>\n      <div class=\"math-editor-tools\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Formula tools\">\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" data-variant=\"outline\" data-size=\"sm\" data-math-command=\"fraction\"\n          >Fraction</button\n        >\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" data-variant=\"outline\" data-size=\"sm\" data-math-command=\"power\">Power</button>\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" data-variant=\"ghost\" data-size=\"sm\" data-math-command=\"undo\">Undo</button>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"paper-equation\">\n      <figure class=\"math-renderer\" id=\"pmi-yours\" aria-label=\"Equation 2: your model\">\n        <code class=\"math-renderer-source\">P(t) = \\frac{K}{1 + A e^{-rt}}</code>\n      </figure>\n      <span class=\"paper-equation-num\">(2)</span>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pmi-s3\">\n    <h2 id=\"pmi-s3\"><span class=\"paper-num\">3&nbsp;</span>The rate of change</h2>\n    <p\n      >How fast does the population grow? Differentiate (1) with respect to t. The Compute Engine applies the quotient,\n      sum, product and exponential rules; the result holds wherever the denominator is not zero - a condition read from\n      the input, which for A &gt; 0 always holds.</p\n    >\n    <section class=\"math-compute\" aria-label=\"Differentiate the logistic model with respect to t\">\n      <label class=\"label\" for=\"pmi-rate-source\">P(t)</label>\n      <textarea class=\"math-compute-source\" id=\"pmi-rate-source\">\\frac{K}{1+Ae^{-rt}}</textarea>\n      <div class=\"math-compute-tools\">\n        <button class=\"btn\" type=\"button\" data-math-run>Differentiate with respect to t</button>\n      </div>\n      \n    </section>\n  </section>\n</article>\n","individual":false}]
